        {
          "name": "comment",
          "value": "<p><strong>PURPOSE</strong></p><p>Marks an order as \"Successfully Processed\" after the approved order has been successfully pushed to the downstream accounting system. Represents the happy-path final state of the Order Review process.</p><p><strong>WHAT THIS WORKFLOW DOES</strong></p><p>1. Re-fetch the Order</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Retrieves the latest order details from Salesforce.</p><p>2. Prepare the Data</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Reshapes the Salesforce response into the flat structure used by the orders table.</p><p>3. Apply Status</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Sets the order's status field to \"Successfully Processed\".</p><p>4. Update Database</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Saves the change so the dashboard shows the order as complete.</p><p><strong>WHEN IT RUNS</strong></p><p>Triggered after the Push Approved Order workflow returns push_result = success.</p><p><strong>OUTCOME</strong></p><p>Terminal state — the order has completed its entire review and processing journey successfully. No further automated steps run.</p>",
          "widget": "textarea_rich"
        }
      ],
      "engine": "scala,pyspark,polars,agent",
      "inputAnchors": [],
      "outputAnchors": [],
      "agentTool": false
